                {"role": "user", "content": "Out of curiosity, what does halal actually mean in Islam?"},
                {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\"response\": \"Halal (Arabic \\u062d\\u0644\\u0627\\u0644) simply means \\u201cpermissible\\u201d or \\u201clawful\\u201d in Islam. It\\u2019s a term used to describe anything that\\u2019s allowed under Islamic law\\u2014especially food, drinks, medicines, cosmetics, and other products. For something to be halal, it must meet a few key criteria:\\n\\n1. **No prohibited ingredients** \\u2013 No pork, blood, alcohol, or any animal that wasn\\u2019t slaughtered according to Islamic rites.  \\n2. **Proper preparation** \\u2013 The animal (if used) must be slaughtered by a Muslim (or a person of the People of the Book) with a swift, humane cut while invoking God\\u2019s name.  \\n3. **Cleanliness** \\u2013 The production process must avoid cross\\u2011contamination with haram (forbidden) substances.  \\n4. **Ethical considerations** \\u2013 Many scholars also look at the overall ethical impact, such as humane treatment of animals and fair trade practices.\\n\\nIn everyday life, you\\u2019ll often see a halal certification logo on products, showing that a trusted certifying body has verified the item meets these standards.\\n\\nIs there a particular type of halal product you\\u2019re curious about or need help finding? I\\u2019m happy to search our database for you!\", \"matched\": [], \"relevant\": []}"},
